- The application builds and runs correctly with the new integration

## How Speed Insights Works

Once deployed to Vercel:
1. Speed Insights will automatically track Core Web Vitals (CLS, FID, LCP, FCP, TTFB, INP)
2. Data will appear in the Vercel dashboard after users visit the site
3. No additional configuration is needed - the integration is automatic
4. The function injects the necessary tracking scripts at runtime

## Next Steps for Users

1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings → Speed Insights)
3. Wait for user visits to accumulate data
4. View performance metrics in the Vercel dashboard

## Technical Notes

- The `injectSpeedInsights()` function is called during application bootstrap
- It automatically handles script injection and metric collection
- Debug mode is automatically enabled in development environments
- Production deployments will use optimized tracking
- The integration is non-blocking and won't affect application performance

## Documentation References

- Official Quickstart: https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
- Package Documentation: https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/package
- Implementation follows the generic function approach recommended for frameworks without explicit support
